<% content_for :title, "MCP Server Integration - Demo Selection" %>

<div class="container py-5">

  <%# Hero Section %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
      <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">
        <i class="bi bi-hdd-network text-primary me-2"></i>
        MCP Server Integration
      </h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted mb-4">
        Learn how to connect AIsuru AI agents to external data sources via MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers.
        Explore demos to see how agents can query databases and manage files in real time.
      </p>
      <div class="badge bg-info text-white fs-6 px-3 py-2">
        <i class="bi bi-book me-1"></i>
        SYS-06 Module - System Integrator Course
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Demo Card - Single centered %>
  <div class="row g-4 mb-5 justify-content-center">

    <%# Demo 1 Card: MongoDB via MCP %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00684a 0%, #13aa52 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-1-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 1: MongoDB via MCP
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-success-subtle text-success me-2">MCP Server</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark">MongoDB</span>
            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning">ngrok</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">AI Agent queries MongoDB through MCP</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Connect an AIsuru AI agent to a MongoDB database using a MCP server integrated in the platform.
            The agent can read, search and analyze data from your collections in real time.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Run MongoDB locally with Docker
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Expose MongoDB over HTTPS using ngrok
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Configure the MCP server integration in AIsuru
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Chat with your agent to query live data
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>MCP Server (AIsuru)</strong> &rarr; <strong>ngrok HTTPS</strong> &rarr; <strong>MongoDB (Docker)</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo1_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00684a 0%, #13aa52 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 1
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Demo 2 Card: MySQL via MCP Server %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e85d04 0%, #f48c06 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-2-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 2: MySQL via MCP Server
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-danger-subtle text-danger me-2">MCP Server</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark">MySQL</span>
            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning">ngrok</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">AI Agent manages MySQL through self-hosted MCP</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Deploy a self-hosted MCP server (from npm package) that allows an AIsuru AI agent to
            perform CRUD operations on a MySQL database. The agent can query, insert, update and delete data in real time.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Deploy MCP server from npm package
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Run MySQL database with Docker
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Configure MCP server to connect to MySQL
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              See real-time database changes via agent
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>ngrok HTTPS</strong> &rarr; <strong>MCP Server (npm)</strong> &rarr; <strong>MySQL (Docker)</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo2_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e85d04 0%, #f48c06 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 2
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Demo 3 Card: Filesystem MCP Server %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00a4ef 0%, #0078d4 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-3-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 3: Filesystem MCP Server
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-primary-subtle text-primary me-2">MCP Server</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark">Filesystem</span>
            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning">ngrok</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">AI Agent manages files through MCP</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Connect an AIsuru AI agent to a custom filesystem MCP server. The agent can create,
            read, write and list files in a shared workspace directory.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Build a custom MCP server in Node.js
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Expose filesystem operations via MCP protocol
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Deploy MCP server with Docker Compose
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              See real-time file changes in the workspace
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>ngrok HTTPS</strong> &rarr; <strong>MCP Server (Node.js)</strong> &rarr; <strong>Shared Filesystem</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo3_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #00a4ef 0%, #0078d4 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 3
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Demo 4 Card: MCP Scheduler + MCP Persistence %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-4-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 4: MCP Scheduler + Persistence
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-purple-subtle text-dark me-2" style="background-color: #f0e9fa;">MCP Server</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark">Scheduler</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark">Persistence</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">AI Agent schedules tasks and persists data</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Connect an AIsuru AI agent to the platform's built-in Scheduler and Persistence MCP
            servers &mdash; no self-hosted backend required. The agent can schedule follow-up actions
            and store structured data across sessions.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Schedule a tool call to run at a later time
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Persist structured data across turns and sessions
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Configure the Scheduler and Persistence MCP servers in AIsuru
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>MCP Scheduler (AIsuru)</strong> + <strong>MCP Persistence (AIsuru)</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo4_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 4
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Demo 5 Card: Agent as MCP %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-5-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 5: Agent as MCP
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark me-2">Agent Link</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark me-2">Agent to agent</span>
            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning">No local infra</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">One agent becomes the tool of another</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Expose an AIsuru agent as an <strong>MCP server</strong> through AIsuru Agent Link, then
            register it as a custom MCP on a second agent. With a Builder token, the second agent can
            even rewrite the first one&rsquo;s prompt.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Generate the two MCP tokens of an agent
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Tell apart the Consumer token and the Builder token
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Register a custom MCP server on a second agent
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Watch one agent modify another agent's prompt
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>Assistant Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>MCP Server (AIsuru Agent Link)</strong> &rarr; <strong>Expert Agent</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo5_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f766e 0%, #14b8a6 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 5
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Demo 6 Card: OAuth / API Connector %>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card h-100 shadow-lg border-0 card-hover">
        <div class="card-header text-white py-3" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
          <h4 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-6-circle me-2"></i>
            Demo 6: OAuth / API Connector
          </h4>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
          <div class="mb-4">
            <span class="badge bg-danger-subtle text-danger me-2">OAuth2</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark me-2">REST API</span>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark me-2">OpenAPI</span>
            <span class="badge bg-warning-subtle text-warning">ngrok</span>
          </div>

          <h5 class="card-title">AI Agent calls your REST API</h5>
          <p class="card-text text-muted">
            Connect an existing HTTP/REST API to an AIsuru agent without writing a line of code.
            Point the connector at an OpenAPI spec and every endpoint becomes a tool, with the
            OAuth2 token requested, cached and renewed for you.
          </p>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">What you'll learn:</h6>
          <ul class="list-unstyled small">
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Run a REST API with OAuth2 client credentials in Docker
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Expose it over HTTPS using ngrok
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Import every endpoint from the OpenAPI spec, no JSON by hand
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-check-circle text-success me-2"></i>
              Watch the agent read data and write it back
            </li>
          </ul>

          <hr>

          <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture:</h6>
          <p class="small text-muted mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-diagram-3 text-primary me-1"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong> &rarr; <strong>OAuth/API Connector</strong> &rarr; <strong>ngrok HTTPS</strong> &rarr; <strong>FastAPI ERP (Docker)</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-footer bg-white border-0 p-4">
          <%= link_to demo6_path, class: "btn btn-lg w-100 text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-play-circle me-2"></i>
            Start Demo 6
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
